 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per sample, as it is a procedural function.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$, no data structures required.
-- **Performance:** Fast to evaluate, but the addition of noise functions and helical calculations can increase computational cost compared to simple radial falloffs.
-- **Strengths:** Simple to implement, produces realistic swirling smoke columns, easily animatable.
-- **Limitations:** Lacks complex internal structures (e.g., eddies) unless enhanced with noise. The helical displacement may not accurately simulate all types of turbulent flow.
-- **When to use:** When a simple, animated smoke column with swirling motion is needed.
-- **When not to use:** When complex, non-helical turbulence or detailed internal structures are required.
